# transaction-log.md is an append-only log: `mise run commit` inserts every
# entry at one fixed anchor (<!-- TRANSACTION_LOG_START -->), and the file is
# cleared only on push to main. Any two branches cut before either merges
# therefore both write the same line, and conflict structurally rather than
# by bad luck — harmonic-forge#376, live incident: feat/366-cross-family-helper
# and feat/371-receipt-integrity, where F371's PR sat mergeStateStatus DIRTY
# with CI never triggering.
#
# merge=union keeps BOTH sides' added lines instead of raising a conflict.
# Correct here specifically because entry order carries no meaning and each
# entry embeds its own commit message and diff content, so two sides never
# add an identical line. Do not extend this to files where line order or
# uniqueness matters — union resolves silently, so a bad fit produces a
# wrong merge with no conflict to notice.
transaction-log.md merge=union
